    title: 'BYU ECE Student Earns Second Place at National SHPE Poster Competition',
    description:
      'Electrical and computer engineering student Alejandro Pelaez earned second place in the undergraduate poster competition at the Society of Hispanic Professional Engineers…',
    date: '2026-10-30',
    author: 'Allyson Gibson',
    sourceUrl:
      'https://ece.byu.edu/byu-ece-student-earns-second-place-at-national-shpe-poster-competition',
    content:
      "Electrical and computer engineering student Alejandro Pelaez earned second place in the undergraduate poster competition at the Society of Hispanic Professional Engineers (SHPE) National Convention, one of the largest gatherings of Hispanic engineers in the world.\n\nPelaez, a senior in BYU's Electrical and Computer Engineering Department, was recognized for his research on real-time autonomous aerial planning. His work attracted significant interest from judges and industry professionals attending the conference.\n\nThe undergraduate poster competition brought together engineering students from across the United States representing multiple engineering disciplines. According to conference organizers, the judging was highly competitive, requiring an additional round of evaluation among finalists before selecting the winners.\n\nFor his achievement, Pelaez received a $750 award and represented BYU engineering and undergraduate research with distinction. Dr. Randy Beard is his research advisor.\n\n![BYU ECE Student Earns Second Place at National SHPE Poster Competition image 2](/news/byu-ece-student-earns-second-place-at-national-shpe-poster-competition/image-02.jpg)",
