      "According to U.S. News, the rankings are based on “expert opinions about program excellence and statistical indicators that measure the quality of a school's faculty, research and students.” The data comes from statistical surveys from more than 2,012 programs and reputation surveys from more than 20,500 academics and professionals.\n\nEach year, U.S. News releases professional program rankings in six different areas: business, education, engineering, law, medicine and nursing. They also rank specialties within those areas.\n\nFind all badge-elligible schools here (opens in a new tab) Find graduate “Best Engineering Schools” here (opens in a new tab)",
